{% comment %}
  Loads a stylesheet without blocking the first paint.

  `stylesheet_tag` emits a plain <link rel="stylesheet">, which is
  render-blocking even inside <body> - the browser stops building the render
  tree until it arrives. For sections below the fold that cost buys nothing.

  This uses `rel="preload" as="style"` rather than the more common
  `media="print"` trick on purpose. Both are non-blocking, but `media="print"`
  is fetched at the *lowest* priority, so on a slow connection the sheet can
  land after the visitor has already scrolled the section into view - which
  trades a render-blocking request for a visible restyle and a layout shift.
  `preload as="style"` is non-blocking *and* high priority, so it is in hand
  well before the section is reached.

  Only use this for below-the-fold sections. Above-the-fold CSS must stay
  blocking, otherwise the section paints unstyled first and shifts.

  Usage:
    {% render 'stylesheet-async', file: 'component-card.css' %}
{% endcomment %}
<link
  rel="preload"
  as="style"
  href="{{ file | asset_url }}"
  onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'"
>
<noscript>{{ file | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}</noscript>
